      "confidence": 0.75,
      "curator_note": "Same retro-[2+2] cleavage of the cyclobutanol molecular ion, but CHARGE MIGRATION: the charge+odd electron end up on the ethylene fragment (H2C=CH2+.) and neutral vinyl alcohol leaves. Book draws 4 fishhook barbs (two per cleaved bond, bonds <1,4> and <2,5>) -- moves <1,2,3,4> are those drawn. Move <5> (O odd electron -> EXTERNAL) is a curator bookkeeping hook, NOT drawn: the ethylene radical cation is delocalised so it is written as its neutral skeleton with the +. recorded in the species charge/radical fields (per the sanctioned EQ4.7 convention), and move <5> balances the single-electron count as the O(+.) site is neutralised."
    },
