      "confidence": 0.45,
      "curator_note": "Cross-links to IMS_4_4_row2 (charge-migration partner of row1). Same MISMATCH as 4.4a: the DFS uses an O-in-ring oxolane precursor and cleaves an O-C bond, whereas the book is exocyclic-OH cyclobutanol cleaving two C-C bonds. See rule_mismatches. | RECHECK 2026-07-24: charge-MIGRATION row. The 4 drawn retro-/elimination barbs yield neutral-connectivity fragments; the +. resides on the ETHYLENE fragment, a delocalized pi radical cation with no localized Lewis structure. It is therefore carried in the charge/radical_electrons fields (neutral-skeleton SMILES), and the odd electron leaving the O is encoded as an `external` location -- the same non-localizable-radical-cation convention as eqs 4.3/4.5/4.8, NOT a literal second ionization. semantics set to net_fragmentation because the migration electron flow is not drawn."
